+# Architecture Plan: WebSocket Graceful Shutdown Notification
+
+## Topic
+`ws-graceful-shutdown-notification` — `docs/arch/ws-graceful-shutdown-notification.md`
+
+Adds an automatic, library-agnostic "server is going away" notification for connected WebSocket
+clients, delivered immediately before their connection is closed as part of the framework's
+existing graceful-shutdown sequence (`NestApplication.dispose()` → `SocketModule.close()` →
+`adapter.close(server)`).
+
+## Implementation Order
+
+All 3 cells are **created anew** — no CODEMANIFEST previously existed for `packages/websockets/`,
+`packages/platform-socket.io/`, or `packages/platform-ws/` (confirmed via `goga schema`).
+
+1. **`packages/websockets/adapters`** — no Imports; the shared base type (`AbstractWsAdapter`).
+   Designed first per leaves-to-root ordering.
+2. **`packages/platform-socket.io/adapters`** — depends on cell 1 (imports `AbstractWsAdapter`,
+   mutated as `AbstractWsAdapter::IoAdapter`).
+3. **`packages/platform-ws/adapters`** — depends on cell 1 (imports `AbstractWsAdapter`, mutated as
+   `AbstractWsAdapter::WsAdapter`). No dependency on cell 2; may be implemented in either order
+   relative to it once cell 1 exists.
+
+## Artifacts
+
+### 1. `packages/websockets/adapters/CODEMANIFEST` (new)
+
+```
+Annotations: |
+  Defines Nest's WS-transport adapter boundary: the abstract surface every WebSocket
+  platform integration (socket.io, ws, and others) must implement so the rest of
+  the framework (SocketModule, gateway binding) can create servers, wire client
+  connect/disconnect, and tear servers down without knowing which underlying WS
+  library is in use.
+
+---
+
+"AbstractWsAdapter(appOrHttpServer: Object<string, any> | undefined)":
+  location: ws-adapter.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Abstract base class for platform WS adapters. Concrete subclasses (socket.io,
+    ws, and others) wrap a specific WS library instance behind this common
+    surface.
+
+    `appOrHttpServer`: an existing Nest application/HTTP server to bind to, or
+    undefined to let the subclass create its own
+
+    Algorithm:
+    1. Concrete subclasses call the base constructor with an already-created
+       application/HTTP-server reference, or let the base class leave it
+       undefined
+    2. `forceCloseConnections` is a plain flag subclasses read during close/dispose
+       to decide whether to hard-close connections sharing the application's own
+       HTTP server
+  properties:
+    "forceCloseConnections -> bool": |
+      Whether server teardown should forcibly close connections that share the
+      application's own HTTP server, rather than leaving them to close
+      gracefully on their own.
+  methods:
+    "bindClientConnect(server: any, callback: Function)": |
+      Register `callback` to run whenever a new client connects to `server`.
+    "bindClientDisconnect(client: any, callback: Function)": |
+      Register `callback` to run once when `client` disconnects.
+    "close(server: any)": |
+      Stop accepting new connections on `server` and shut it down.
+
+      Algorithm:
+      1. Call `notifyClientsOnShutdown` to give currently connected clients a
+         chance to receive a heads-up message before teardown
+      2. If `server` exposes a close method, call it and await completion
+    "dispose()": |
+      No-op by default; subclasses override to release adapter-wide resources
+      (e.g. extra HTTP servers they created).
+    "create(port: number, options: Object<string, any> | undefined) -> server: any": |
+      Abstract. Create and return a concrete WS server instance bound to `port`,
+      shaped by `options`.
+    "bindMessageHandlers(client: any, handlers: Array<Object<string, any>>, transform: Function)": |
+      Abstract. Wire `client`'s incoming messages to `handlers`, passing each
+      through `transform`.
+    "notifyClientsOnShutdown(server: any)": |
+      No-op by default. Subclasses override to broadcast a small "server is
+      going away" message to every client currently connected to `server`,
+      called by `close` immediately before the server actually stops
+      accepting/serving connections.
+
+      Requirements:
+      - Must not throw — a failure to notify must never block or fail the
+        shutdown sequence itself
+
+---
+
+Author: Goga
+CreatedAt: 17/09/26
+Description: |
+  Documents the abstract WS-transport adapter contract that decouples the
+  framework's gateway layer from any specific WebSocket library, mirroring
+  AbstractHttpAdapter for the WS transport. Concrete platform packages
+  (socket.io, ws) mutate this type rather than the framework depending on them
+  directly, and every subclass automatically inherits the shutdown-notification
+  template method via `close`.
+```
+
+`.usages/` files: none (no independent external consumer beyond the two mutating sibling cells;
+matches the existing `packages/core/adapters` cell, which also has none).
+
+---
+
+### 2. `packages/platform-socket.io/adapters/CODEMANIFEST` (new)
+
+```
+Imports:
+  - Types:
+      - AbstractWsAdapter
+    From: packages/websockets/adapters
+
+Annotations: |
+  Concrete `AbstractWsAdapter` implementation over the socket.io library: the
+  default WS platform used by the socket.io platform package.
+
+---
+
+"AbstractWsAdapter::IoAdapter(appOrHttpServer: Object<string, any> | undefined)":
+  location: io-adapter.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Wraps socket.io's Server/Namespace behind the `AbstractWsAdapter` contract
+    from Imports.
+
+    `appOrHttpServer`: an existing Nest application/HTTP server to bind the
+    socket.io server to, or undefined
+  methods:
+    "create(port: number, options: Object<string, any> | undefined) -> server: any": |
+      Create (or resolve, for a namespaced request against an already-created
+      server) a socket.io Server or Namespace.
+    "createIOServer(port: number, options: Object<string, any> | undefined) -> server: any": |
+      Construct a new socket.io Server, bound to the shared HTTP server when
+      `port` is 0 and one is available, otherwise listening on `port` directly.
+    "bindMessageHandlers(socket: any, handlers: Array<Object<string, any>>, transform: Function)": |
+      Wire each handler in `handlers` to the matching socket.io event on
+      `socket`, running responses through `transform` and emitting/acking the
+      result.
+    "mapPayload(payload: any) -> mapped: Object<string, any>": |
+      Split an incoming socket.io event payload into its data and an optional
+      acknowledgement callback.
+    "bindClientDisconnect(client: any, callback: Function)": |
+      Register `callback` to run once when `client`'s socket.io disconnect
+      event fires, passing the disconnect reason.
+    "close(server: any)": |
+      Algorithm:
+      1. If `forceCloseConnections` is set and `server` shares the application's
+         own underlying HTTP server, call `notifyClientsOnShutdown` and return
+         without closing `server` directly — the shared HTTP server's own close
+         (elsewhere in the shutdown sequence) will terminate these connections
+      2. Otherwise, delegate to the base close from `AbstractWsAdapter`, which
+         itself calls `notifyClientsOnShutdown` before closing `server`
+
+      Requirements:
+      - `notifyClientsOnShutdown` must run exactly once per close call,
+        regardless of which branch is taken
+    "notifyClientsOnShutdown(server: any)": |
+      Broadcast a shutdown event carrying a small heads-up message to every
+      socket currently connected to `server`, so socket.io clients receive it
+      before the connection closes.
+
+---
+
+Author: Goga
+CreatedAt: 17/09/26
+Description: |
+  Documents the socket.io platform adapter as a concrete mutation of
+  `AbstractWsAdapter`, showing how a WS platform package plugs into the adapter
+  boundary and broadcasts a shutdown notification to every connected socket
+  before the underlying server closes.
+```
+
+`.usages/` files: none (matches `packages/platform-express/adapters`, which also has none).
+
+---
+
+### 3. `packages/platform-ws/adapters/CODEMANIFEST` (new)
+
+```
+Imports:
+  - Types:
+      - AbstractWsAdapter
+    From: packages/websockets/adapters
+
+Annotations: |
+  Concrete `AbstractWsAdapter` implementation over the `ws` library: the
+  lightweight WS platform used by the ws platform package. Does not support
+  namespaces.
+
+---
+
+"AbstractWsAdapter::WsAdapter(appOrHttpServer: Object<string, any> | undefined, options: Object<string, any> | undefined)":
+  location: ws-adapter.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Wraps one or more raw ws server instances behind the `AbstractWsAdapter`
+    contract from Imports, including support for multiple ws servers sharing a
+    single HTTP server across different paths/ports.
+
+    `appOrHttpServer`: an existing Nest application/HTTP server, or undefined
+    `options`: adapter-level configuration, e.g. a custom message parser
+  methods:
+    "create(port: number, options: Object<string, any> | undefined) -> server: any": |
+      Create a raw ws server, registering it against the shared HTTP server
+      when appropriate for the given port/path/server combination.
+    "bindMessageHandlers(client: any, handlers: Array<Object<string, any>>, transform: Function)": |
+      Wire `client`'s incoming messages to the matching handler in `handlers`
+      by parsed event name, sending the transformed result back as a JSON
+      string.
+    "bindMessageHandler(buffer: any, handlersMap: Object<string, any>, transform: Function) -> result: any": |
+      Parse one raw message `buffer`, look up its handler in `handlersMap`, and
+      run it through `transform`.
+    "bindErrorHandler(server: any) -> server: any": |
+      Attach error logging to `server` and to every client it accepts.
+    "bindClientDisconnect(client: any, callback: Function)": |
+      Register `callback` to run once when `client`'s underlying socket close
+      event fires.
+    "close(server: any)": |
+      Algorithm:
+      1. Call `notifyClientsOnShutdown` and await it, so every currently-OPEN
+         client has its shutdown message flushed
+      2. Begin closing `server` and, concurrently, force-terminate every
+         remaining client in `server.clients`
+      3. Await the server's close completion
+
+      Requirements:
+      - Notification must complete (or fail silently) before the terminate
+        loop runs, so the message isn't discarded by the immediately-following
+        hard close
+    "dispose()": |
+      Close every extra HTTP server this adapter created (skipping the
+      application's own), then clear the internal registries.
+    "setMessageParser(parser: Function)": |
+      Replace the function used to parse incoming raw message buffers into
+      {event, data}.
+    "notifyClientsOnShutdown(server: any)": |
+      Send a small JSON-encoded {event, data} heads-up payload to every client
+      in `server.clients` whose readyState is OPEN, waiting for each send to be
+      flushed to the socket before returning.
+
+      Requirements:
+      - A send failure for one client must not prevent notifying or closing
+        the others
+
+---
+
+Author: Goga
+CreatedAt: 17/09/26
+Description: |
+  Documents the ws-library platform adapter as a second concrete mutation of
+  `AbstractWsAdapter`, alongside the socket.io adapter, showing the same
+  shutdown-notification contract satisfied over a lower-level WS library: a
+  flushed JSON message per open client precedes the existing hard-terminate
+  close path.
+```
+
+`.usages/` files: none (matches `packages/platform-fastify/adapters`, which also has none).
+
+## Dependency Map
+
+```
+packages/websockets/adapters (AbstractWsAdapter)
+        │
+        ├──(AbstractWsAdapter)──> packages/platform-socket.io/adapters (IoAdapter)
+        │
+        └──(AbstractWsAdapter)──> packages/platform-ws/adapters (WsAdapter)
+```
+
+## Verification Checklist
+
+- `goga lint` passes with 0 errors across all 3 new cells (DSL syntax, key casing, signature rules).
+- `goga contract packages/websockets/adapters packages/platform-socket.io/adapters packages/platform-ws/adapters`
+  shows implementation signatures matching the CODEMANIFEST for every listed entity/method once code is written.
+- `AbstractWsAdapter.close()` calls `notifyClientsOnShutdown(server)` before `server.close(resolve)`.
+- `IoAdapter.close()` calls `notifyClientsOnShutdown` exactly once regardless of the
+  `forceCloseConnections` branch taken (no double-emit).
+- `WsAdapter.close()` awaits `notifyClientsOnShutdown(server)` fully before the existing
+  `ws.terminate()` loop runs.
+- No changes to `bindClientConnect`, `bindClientDisconnect`, `bindMessageHandlers`,
+  `bindMessageHandler`, `create`, `createIOServer`, `mapPayload`, `bindErrorHandler`,
+  `setMessageParser`, `dispose` signatures or behavior — only `close` gains a new leading step,
+  and `notifyClientsOnShutdown` is newly added.
+- No changes to `packages/core/nest-application.ts`, `packages/core/nest-application-context.ts`,
+  or `packages/websockets/socket-module.ts` — the existing `dispose()` → `socketModule.close()` →
+  `adapter.close(server)` call chain is the delivery mechanism and needs no modification.
+- Unit tests: a gateway with 0 connected clients at shutdown observes no behavior change; an app
+  with no WS adapter registered (`SocketModule.close()`'s existing early-returns) observes no
+  behavior change; existing connect/disconnect/message-handling tests continue to pass unmodified.
